    "quote": "For the $N$-armed stochastic bandit problem, Thompson Sampling algorithm has expected regret $$\\Ex[{\\cal R}(T)] \\leq (1+\\epsilon) \\sum_{i=2}^N \\frac{\\ln T}{d(\\mu_i,\\mu_1)} \\Delta_i+ O(\\frac{N}{\\epsilon^2})  $$ in time $T$, where $d(\\mu_i,\\mu_1)=...$. The big-Oh notation in above assumes $\\mu_i, \\Delta_i, i=1, \\ldots, N$ to be constants."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Leading term is exact with constant (1+eps); only the additive N/eps^2 term is in big-O (hiding mu_i, Delta_i dependence). Analysis is for Bernoulli rewards, extended to [0,1] via the Bernoulli-trial reduction of Agrawal & Goyal 2012. Regret defined via means, so pseudo-regret. Unique optimal arm assumed w.l.o.g."
